% The four binding kinds, in the positions M2 can use them.

### name: bind.column.typed
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "total", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T * 2
--- expect
(`o`.`total` * 2)
===
### name: bind.value.scalar-is-quoted-by-default
--- note
A host-supplied value is TEXT unless it says otherwise. Guessing from the
characters would emit a product code of "00123" as the number 123.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"CODE": {"kind": "value", "value": "00123"}}
--- source
CODE
--- expect
'00123'
===
### name: bind.value.numeric-when-declared
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"LIMIT": {"kind": "value", "value": "100", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
LIMIT
--- expect
100
===
### name: bind.value.indexed
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"L": {"kind": "value", "value": {"1": "a", "2": "b"}}}
--- source
L[2]
--- expect
'b'
===
### name: bind.value.list-is-not-a-scalar
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"L": {"kind": "value", "value": {"1": "a", "2": "b"}}}
--- source
L
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: bind.columns.indexed-positionally
--- note
Keys are "1", "2", … exactly as `,` builds them.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}, {"table": "x", "column": "b", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
V[2] > 0
--- expect
(`x`.`b` > 0)
===
### name: bind.columns.index-out-of-range
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
V[5]
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING 1:2
===
### name: bind.relation.field-is-a-column-reference
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"I": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
I["qty"] > 0
--- expect
(`oi`.`qty` > 0)
